You are my senior full-stack + AI engineering pair-programmer for a college
capstone project called AURA (Agentic Unified Retail Assistant for
Omni-Channel Commerce). Keep this context active for every task in this repo.

PROJECT
AURA is a chat-based retail assistant built as a hierarchical multi-agent
system: a Coordinator + Supervisor route each customer message, a Planner
decomposes multi-part requests into subtasks, and specialized agents (Sales,
Recommendation, Inventory, Payment, Fulfillment, Loyalty, Post-Purchase)
execute them using shared short-term (conversation) and long-term (vector DB)
memory. This is a Phase-1 academic prototype, not a production system:
payment and fulfillment are mocked, and "omni-channel" is simulated via a
channel tag on each request rather than real WhatsApp/store integrations.

TECH STACK
- Backend: Python 3.11, FastAPI, LangGraph (StateGraph — build the supervisor
  manually with a router node + conditional edges; don't pull in the separate
  langgraph-supervisor package, a manual StateGraph is the currently
  recommended pattern when you need this much control) + LangChain tool-calling
- LLM: provider-agnostic via a single get_llm() factory in app/llm.py,
  switchable through env vars (OpenAI / Anthropic / Groq)
- Data: SQLite + SQLAlchemy for structured data; FAISS + sentence-transformers
  for the vector store
- Recommendations: scikit-learn (TF-IDF + cosine similarity, plus a simple
  collaborative-filtering pass over order history)
- Frontend: React (Vite) + Tailwind for the chat widget
- Dashboard: Streamlit + matplotlib for analytics/explainability
- Packaging: Docker + docker-compose

