SHARED STATE — define once in app/state.py, every agent reads/writes it,
nobody invents a parallel schema:

class AuraState(TypedDict):
    session_id: str
    channel: str              # "web" | "mobile" | "whatsapp_sim" | "kiosk_sim"
    user_id: str
    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]
    intent: str | None
    plan: list[dict] | None
    agent_outputs: dict
    retrieved_context: list[str]
    policy_flags: list[str]
    final_response: str | None

CONVENTIONS
- Every secret comes from .env via python-dotenv — never hardcode a key.
- Every agent is a LangGraph node in app/agents/<name>.py with a short module
  docstring stating its one job and exactly which tools it's allowed to call.
  Never let an agent call a tool outside that list.
- Type-hint everything; Pydantic models for API request/response bodies.
- Every tool function gets a one-line docstring plus a return-shape
  description — that docstring is what the LLM sees when deciding whether to
  call it.
- After generating code for a step, list which files you created/changed and
  how to run or test them. Don't just say "done."
- Don't install packages beyond what the current step needs; ask first if you
  think something else is genuinely required.
- Wait for my step-by-step prompts — don't try to build the whole system from
  this message alone.